ion for speaking out  this hospital worker asked us to shield  her identity I think we have it worse  than a traditional hospital because our  patient's can at any given time  become violent you know we have patients  that don't understand the grasp of  coughing into your arm or sneezing into  your arm I am wearing my seahawks cloth  mask a nurse Sharon Behn third told CBS  News the hospital only recently provided  some protective equipment  after weeks of forbidding staff from  bringing their own according to internal  hospital emails nobody was allowed to  wear masks if they see you wearing masks  they will tell you to take it off close  Mariya Claudio's family bought this used  RV anticipating she will need to self  isolate in the weeks ahead like her  coworkers Claudio says she is committed  to the patients who are among society's  most isolated they rely on us for  everything they are locked in there we  have the keys we have all the power so  we have the responsibility to take care  of them  spokesperson for Western State told CBS  News that they moved quickly to protect  their high-risk population limiting  infections and now even more aggressive  actions are being taken CBS went back to  the hospital staff we interviewed who  said the changes don't come close to  addressing their ongoing concerns Tony  well if the allegations are true we do  hope those changes are made and swiftly  Katherine thank you very much
 

